    "evidence_text": "Characterization of two classes of small molecule inhibitors of Arp2/3 complex\n\nCK-0993548 inserts into the hydrophobic core of Arp3 and alters its conformation.\n\nBoth classes of compounds inhibit formation of actin filament comet tails by Listeria and podosomes by monocytes.\n\nFormins at the Junction.\n\nFormins dynamically shape the actin cytoskeleton and have various functions within cells.\n\nAluminum fluoride stimulates surface protrusions in cells overexpressing the ARF6 GTPase\n\nArp2/3 complex inhibition radically alters lamellipodial actin architecture, suspended cell shape, and the cell spreading process\n\nNucleating actin for invasion\n\nInvadopodia are matrix-degrading membrane protrusions in invasive carcinoma cells.\n\nThe mechanisms regulating invadopodium assembly and maturation are not understood.\n\nCortactin directly binds cofilin and inhibits its severing activity.\n\nSequential signals toward podosome formation in NIH-src cells\n\nDespite their significant physiological importance, the molecular mechanism of podosome formation is largely unknown.\n\nIn this study, we investigated the molecular mechanisms of podosome formation.\n\nRho, Rac and Cdc42 regulate actin organization and cell adhesion in macrophages.",
